# Security hardening

## Beta 0 identity boundary (invite-only)

Persisted portfolios/strategies for Beta accounts use **Supabase Auth + Postgres
RLS** (`supabase/schema.sql`). Sign-up requires a **one-time invite code**.
Admin Captain (`profiles.role = admin`) vs beta. Local and Cloudflare share the
same Supabase project when env vars match.

- SPA: prefers Worker `GET /api/auth/config` (from `SUPABASE_URL` /
  `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` secrets). Optional local bake: `VITE_SUPABASE_*`
- Worker: `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (auth config + JWT check on
  `/api/market/*` when configured; set `MARKET_AUTH_REQUIRED=false` for open
  local market proxy)
- Demo Captain (`ENABLE_DEMO_GATE=true`) is **legacy only** — not a save path
  for personal holdings
- Anon key is public by design (RLS enforces access); do not ship service-role
  keys to the client

## STOP and remind before

- Real brokerage/account connections (Webull, E*Trade, MooMoo, Plaid, OAuth)
- Putting **unauthenticated** or shared-demo password saves in front of real
  personal/financial data
- Shipping secrets in the SPA bundle

## What to say if someone proposes Demo-persisted real books

> "Demo Captain is retired for saved Beta work. Personal strategies/holdings go
> behind invite-only Supabase accounts with RLS. Want to issue an invite and use
> Admin Captain instead?"

Do not silently put real-data persistence back on the B1 demo cookie.

## Portfolio file imports

CSV/XLSX portfolio imports are authenticated Beta-only financial data. Inspect
and parse raw files locally, retain only the explicit transaction allowlist, and
never upload, store, or log raw files, filenames, extra columns, or rejected cell
values. Server persistence revalidates normalized rows behind RLS and an
optimistic revision. Brokerage credentials, account/routing numbers, names,
addresses, and other PII are not supported fields; extra columns are stripped,
not heuristically classified.

## Production data preservation

All Supabase and Cloudflare persistence, migration, backfill, binding, and
deployment work must follow `.cursor/rules/production-data-safety.mdc`. RLS and
tenant ownership are conservation invariants: a migration that preserves rows
but changes who can access them is a data-loss incident and must stop rollout.
